@startuml
' REVIEWED_MAIN_2026_05_13: aligned to current merged code; large-investment retained pending simplification merge.
skinparam maxMessageSize 250
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
autonumber

box "Environment A (Dirty / Untrusted)" #LightPink
actor "Initiator" as Init
participant "Squads Web UI\n(Compromisable)" as UI
end box

box "Out-of-Band" #White
participant "Secure Channel\n(Slack / Cognitive Intent)" as OOB
end box

box "Environment B (Secure / Clear Signing)" #LightGreen
actor "Approver" as Appr
participant "Advanced HW Device\n(e.g., GridPlus/Keystone)" as HW
end box

box "Infrastructure" #LightBlue
participant "Private RPC" as RPC
database "Solana Mainnet\n(Squads V4)" as Squads
end box

== Phase 1: Initiation ==
Init -> UI: Draft protocol action
note right of UI: Assume UI is compromised and\nsecretly injects a malicious payload.
UI -> Squads: `Squads::CreateTransaction`
Squads --> UI: Proposal Created (Returns Index ID)

== Phase 2: Out-of-Band Hand-off ==
Init -> OOB: "Please approve Proposal [Index ID].\nIntent: Safe Protocol Upgrade"
note over Init, Appr: If Initiator and Approver are the same person,\nthis step relies on their own cognitive memory.
OOB -> Appr: Communicates Intent and Index ID

== Phase 3: Hardware-Level Fetch & Decode ==
Appr -> HW: Inputs Proposal Index directly into HW Device
HW -> RPC: Fetch account data for Proposal PDA
RPC --> HW: Returns raw, serialized instruction bytes
note right of HW: **FIRMWARE DECODING**\nThe Device natively parses Squads V4 instructions\nusing its isolated Secure Element.

== Phase 4: The Ultimate Manual Check ==
HW -> Appr: Built-in screen displays Human-Readable Intent:\n"Target: Malicious Address"\n"Action: Drain Funds"
note over Appr: **THE ZERO-TRUST CHECK**\nApprover reads the Hardware screen.\nCompares it directly to the OOB intent.\nBecause the UI lied, a discrepancy is found.

== Phase 5: Air-Gapped Rejection ==
Appr -> HW: Refuses to sign (Rejects transaction)
note right of HW: If the text had matched the intent,\nApprover would sign and broadcast via RPC.\nThe attack is successfully neutralized.

@enduml